# IBM Bob Agent Configuration & Code Rules

## Core Operational Rules
1. Never modify code without understanding existing dependencies and running tests.
2. Maintain 100% test pass rate across all test suites after any change.
3. Code changes must prioritize security, performance, and clean maintainability.

## BobGuard Architecture Rules
1. All generated reports (JSON, SARIF) MUST use relative POSIX file paths (e.g., `demo-app/server.js`), NEVER OS-specific absolute paths (no `C:\` or `/Users/`).
2. Error handlers must log detailed error messages server-side (`console.error`) and return generic error payloads to HTTP clients.
3. Do not add external dependencies unless strictly necessary.
4. Remove temporary scratchpad comments, dev annotations, and debug console statements before final submission.